    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c1dc4e0_b53f2a85",
        "filename": "java/sdk.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-23T15:34:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that sdkCore is a separate kind. I think it is orthogonal to that. Core is essentially just a partition of the public API space that relates to the core libraries, i.e. art, i18n and conscrypt.\n\nSimilarly, core_platform is a partition of the \"platform\" kind. Where \"platform\" is more akin to \"private\" than any of the others.\n\nI think core would be better represented by adding another field to sdkSpec, say partition, so core_current would be \"public\", \"core\", \"current\", core_platform would be \"private\", \"core\", \"current\" and system_current would be \"system\", \"\u003csomething, maybe base or an empty string\u003e\", \"current\".",
      "revId": "698d6c7e9b4d435f21000b37fa5a998b2a6a83ce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d35fa20_b606aed3",
        "filename": "java/sdk.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-24T15:22:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. The purpose of this change isn\u0027t to model the logical relationship between the different API surfaces (like the fact that \u0027core_current\u0027 is a subset of \u0027current\u0027). It just aims to tackle the problem that version number is encoded with other information in a single sdk_version string.\n\nExpressing the logical relationship here might be a (near) future refactoring topic though. It would be with the refactoring of the link type check which is causing problem for mainline modules now.",
      "parentUuid": "7c1dc4e0_b53f2a85",
      "revId": "698d6c7e9b4d435f21000b37fa5a998b2a6a83ce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
