      },
      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-25T13:05:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I also felt it difficult. IMHO, interface should be used when there are multiple concrete types implementing it. Using it for things like sdkSpec seems to be an misuse. For struct v.s. *struct, I think the decision could be based on how large the struct is. If it\u0027s small and short-lived, the copy overhead shouldn\u0027t be treated as significant. In that case, *struct might be the worse choice since it gives unnecessary pressure to the heap and GC.",
      "parentUuid": "a7683bed_1e3b281f",
      "revId": "698d6c7e9b4d435f21000b37fa5a998b2a6a83ce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
